{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Environmental News"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Speak Out"}, {"type": "position", "content": 4}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 17}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify and describe events in the news in a range of social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Consonant Blends: the <span class=\"italic\">thr </span>Sound"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p>Consonant clusters like <span class=\"italic\">thr</span> can occur at the beginning of a word in English.</p><p>Practice blending the sound from one consonant sound into the next without adding a vowel sound in between.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read the following words aloud."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">through</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">thrilled</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">thrilling</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">throw</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">throughout</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">throng</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">thrive</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">threat</div>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Ann</span>: What is the greatest threat to the environment right now?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Bob</span>: I'd say that the amount of stuff we throw away every day is staggering. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Stressing New Information"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you want to stress new information, you use different intonation and stress on the \u201cnew\u201d word or idea."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You usually stress content words in a sentence.<br/>Content words are the words that carry the most meaning (nouns, verbs, adjectives, adverbs etc.). "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you use the Simple Past Passive, you stress the <span class=\"strong\">verb in the past participle form</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you want to exchange opinions, you can choose to put the stress and the intonation on the \u201cnew\u201d words. This helps the listener understand that you want to stress that word and that it is related to the opinions they want to give."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the following examples:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">After the first wave of environmental treaties were <span class=\"strong\">signed</span> 20 years ago, awareness programs were <span class=\"strong\">created</span> throughout our country.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Climate change wasn't <span class=\"strong\">studied</span> by scientists as widely as it is now.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">People only started to notice once our cause was <span class=\"strong\">endorsed</span> by movie stars!</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you stress these \u201cnew\u201d words, your voice will rise slightly (intonation). "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "threat"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something likely to cause damage or danger"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: What is the greatest threat to our environment right now?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le17ob04aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear in an interview about climate change."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "throughout"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "all the way through"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(preposition)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Environmental awareness programs were created throughout the country."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le17ob04aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tirelessly"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "without pause"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We need to work tirelessly if we want to defend the environment."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le17ob04aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to thrive"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to succeed; to prosper"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We need to work tirelessly if we want to see these programs thrive."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le17ob04aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "irreparable"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "impossible to repair"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Would you say that irreparable damage was done by the previous generation?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le17ob04aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to endorse"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to support"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: People only started to notice once our cause was endorsed by movie stars!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le17ob04aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "throng"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "large amount or people"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Throngs of people follow movie stars online."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le17